   night 16.28 h. September (the design month): mean night 11.28 h sun down, 10.13 h dark. The longest night is
   16.18 h (December's mean; 16.28 at the solstice), the shortest 7.33 h (June's mean; 7.23 at the solstice).
   Cross-check against PVGIS's mean-day profile (hours with any irradiance, UTC): June 04:00 to 19:59 (16 h),
   September 06:00 to 18:59 (13 h, the last hour at 0.4 W/m2), December 08:00 to 15:59 (8 h, the last at 1.9),
   against 16.7, 12.7 and 7.8 h of sun here: the hourly grid rounds outward by up to an hour each side.

4. THE SOLAR CONTRIBUTION per day, into the kit's system node

   Resource: PVGIS-SARAH2 monthly irradiation 2015 to 2020 on the 40 degree south plane (the pinned monthly file),
   the mean day of each month; the day's shape from PVGIS's DRcalc mean-day profile (2005 to 2020, on fnd/d4energy),
   scaled to the pinned monthly mean. Panel: STC rating x G / 1000 x 0.9417 (PVGIS's own angle, spectral and
   temperature losses, no system loss; maximum-power tracking assumed, which the fixed 17.6 V stage does not do:
   the low bracket takes 0.80). Window: at most 100 W into the stage (REQ-016); above it the stage clips.
   Chain into the node: 0.93 x 0.93 x 0.98 = 0.8476 (bracket 0.782 to 0.926); the panel's 5.68 A at 17.6 V sits
   under F2's and J_SOLAR's 10 A.

