    OFF: slots 1 and 2 with their fans, PCIe switches and drives; both WiFi link cards; the 5G module (no host on
    slot 3); the monitor and HDMI 5 V; the SDR, the camera, the QMX, the Geiger (deferred by D-01); the E72 pair;
    the mixer fans (a shaded, cool night; on in the heat). ON, with traffic: the LoRa module at the planning
    duty (receive plus about 9 percent airtime, 0.3 W) and the RockBLOCK at one session in ten minutes (0.1 W); the
    panel at its declaration's logic share with the lamps at NIGHT's 15 percent (0.82 W, a declaration, not a maker's
    figure). On the tree's model (night_bounds.out, pwr_budget.py imported unchanged): LOW / PLAN / HIGH 11.02 / 16.20 /
    39.67 W at the pack; this page's recount of the rows above 16.63 W; the D rows at the makers' figures 13.77 W.
    The balance uses the model's PLAN 16.20 W. The aged pack carries it 6.7 h at +20 C (9.9 h at LOW, 2.7 h at HIGH),
    against September's 11.3 h of sun-down and 16 h of sun below the load (100 Wp): not a September night alone.
    What it changes: firmware and operator settings only (the KSZ energy-detect mode and the supervisors' 200 MHz
    clock are firmware items to confirm on the generated boards); it is the heat stage after BANK-R1 with six
    loads off or lowered, so it needs BANK-R1 in board B's generator (CONOPS 4c). Cost: none in parts. Mission:
    the monitor, the WiFi link, 5G, Zigbee and two of the three compute modules are off in EVERY HOUR the state runs:
    all 72 hours in sets 1 to 3 of 7, or each hour the panel alone does not carry PS-IDLE-SPEC under 7c's schedule;
    the e-paper and the panel lamps carry the status.

6b. The usable depth of discharge: the graceful line 3.00 V to 2.80 V under load gains 1.9 Wh aged (108 to 110 Wh);
    the 5 percent RSOC reserve then ends the run first at low currents (f_dod capped at 0.95). Cost: none; a
    gauge image and bridge setting (CONOPS 4c's PROVISIONAL threshold). Mission: about 3 minutes more at
    PS-IDLE-SPEC, 7 at the night state; cycle life is the maker's question (the cycle test discharges to 2.65 V).

