6d. A second pack's location inside the fixed case (D-01 deferred it, 'no location found'):
    - east pocket: taken by the ruled pack (6c).
    - west pocket, 58 x 160 x 47.9 (packfit_west.out: A06's pack_fit.py imported unchanged, its zones, bases and
      search): the 4S3P block ALONE fits (X spare 1.35, Y spare 26.50, Z clear 5.20 at the nominal base, 3.99 at the
      worst, under C33 on board B's underside). Board P does NOT fit with it: on top of the block the Z clearance
      is -11.47 with its Keystone 3568 holder and blade (16.17), -5.10 with only its JST XH (9.80), -1.70 even at
      the 8 mm board this page's first issue assumed (-12.68, -6.31, -2.91 at the worst base); at the block's end
      the group is 205.50 long against 160 (Y spare -45.50); at its side 75.42 wide against 58 (X spare -17.42).
      A second board P in the east pocket: the ruled group leaves 34.50 in Y against its 44.0 plus 2.0, and 1.35
      in X: NO. So a west block needs its board P somewhere else, over a harness carrying the pack current and the
      cell taps, and NO such place is found here: the tool models only the two pockets, and the rest of the
      floor is the dock strip and board A's blind-mate gap (13.4 mm, CASE-MARGINS section 3.1), under board P's
      19.8 mm with its holder. The west candidate stays a CANDIDATE with its board P unplaced.
    - the lid: the flat ceiling is 346 x 232, the depth 44.45 at the worst; the QMX tray r2 takes X 83.2 to 171.0
      and stands 33.95 below the ceiling. A ONE-LAYER 4S3P block, two rows of six cells (2 x 56.65 = 113.3 by
      2 x 66.25 + 1 = 133.5 by 19.55 high) or one row of twelve (223.6 x 66.25 x 19.55), on a 2 mm lid plate as
      the tray's, over the lid's west 256 mm of its 346 (X -173 to 83, where D-01's deferred tablet bracket was to go)
      leaves 22.9 mm over the face parts, more than the tray's own room. Mass about 0.65 kg of cells and board
      in the lid; a lid harness across the hinge (the QMX's crossing is already an open item, S-95); the drop
      and vibration hold-down (TEST-PLAN E1, E2) and the lid's own strength are new items. A candidate to CHECK
      against CASE-MARGINS' lid rows (M3, M19) and the face parts' heights (T9, TBD), not a finding: A06's tool
      has no lid pocket, so it cannot be checked in the tree today. Board P rides with that block in the lid.
    Energy: a second 4S3P in parallel doubles every usable figure of section 2 (216 Wh aged at PS-IDLE-SPEC);
    what the combinations of 5d then meet is in that table's last column. Cost ESTIMATE: 12 cells (about 4 EUR
    each at a European distributor, about 50 EUR), a second board P (about 30 EUR fabricated and assembled, the
    JLC BOM's order of magnitude), strip, wrap and a plate: under 150 EUR; a second pack build and a second
    protection commissioning (TEST-PLAN section 5 twice).

6e. The panel and the 100 W window (S-53's route): the table of section 4. Into the node per day, September /
    December: 100 Wp 320 / 90 Wh; 200 Wp 641 / 180 (clipped 0 h in September); 330 Wp 807 / 297 (clipped
    8 h); with no window at all 330 Wp gives 1057 / 297. PS-IDLE-SPEC asks 1027 Wh a day, the reduced mode 753,
    the heat stage 558, the night state 389. So: inside the window no panel carries PS-IDLE-SPEC's day; a
    re-rated path to about 300 W with a 330 Wp panel carries the heat stage's September day and the night state's
    December day; what it cannot do is carry any night, which is the pack's. A panel above about 150 Wp of 12 V
    class also exceeds F2's and J_SOLAR's 10 A at its short circuit (about 6.25 A per 100 Wp, gen_sch_e.py:474),
    so the entry (F2, J_SOLAR, D4, the copper of PV_P) is re-declared with the stage. Cost ESTIMATE: the stage's
    inductor, FETs and sense resistor for 3 x the current, a 20 A fuse and connector, under 40 EUR of parts on
    board E; the panel itself 100 to 300 EUR per 100 Wp class. Mission: none removed; a bigger panel to carry.

    WHAT BOUNDS THE STAGE AS GENERATED: nothing at 100 W. gen_sch_e.py:482-484, U5's pin map: pins 29 to 31 (EXTVCC, CSNOUT, CSPOUT on the 38-lead QFN) on TRK_OUT and pins 32 to 34 (CSNIN, CSPIN, VIN) on PV_P: both current monitors are tied off as the maker says for a monitor 'not in use' (8705af PDF pages 11 and 12), so neither current loop can act; R16 and R17 (10k) hold IMON_IN and IMON_OUT to ground (line 628)
    The tracker delivers the panel's power (gen_sch_e.py:99-101, 580-583) and only board A's front end bounds it, at
    126.9 W drawn (gen_sch_e.py:104-107): 136 W into the stage at 0.93. A 200 Wp panel on a clear day, on pack and
    solar alone, can therefore put about 136 W into it: 7.8 A at 17.6 V, and 8.4 A on TRK_OUT at 15.1 V. The
    model's 100 W clip is a model assumption, conservative for the energy (a mean September day never reaches it:
    the 200 Wp peak is 98.1 W). Two routes, both presented:
    ROUTE A, the window restated: REQ-016's 'at most 100 W into the stage' becomes at most 136 W; PV_P and PV_IN
    from 5.68 A typical and 6.25 A peak to 7.8 A and about 12.5 A (two 100 Wp panels' short circuit); TRK_OUT from
    6.16 A at 15.1 V to 8.4 A (its 10.33 A declaration at the 9 V floor to 14.1 A, which VIN_RAW's 14.10 A already
    carries on board A); F2 and J_SOLAR at 1.25 times the short-circuit current or more, about 15.6 A for a 200 Wp
    panel (the usual photovoltaic practice; no standard for it is held in the tree; a JST-VH is a 10 A part: another
    connector, pick TBD); L1's saturation current, the four FETs' dissipation and R5's sense range re-judged at the higher current
    (the inductor valley limit is 69 mV / 5 mOhm = 13.8 A, gen_sch_e.py:103). D4 and the 25 V window are unchanged
    (two 12 V class panels in parallel keep their open-circuit voltage). More energy on clear days; no change on the
    mean day. It restates a core requirement (REQ-016, SC-36) and board E's declarations.
    ROUTE B, a designed limit that keeps REQ-016's 100 W: the LT8705A's own output current loop (8705af PDF pages 4,
    5, 11, 12 and 19): a sense resistor RSENSE2 between the stage's output and TRK_OUT with CSPOUT (pin 31) on the
    stage side and CSNOUT (pin 30) on TRK_OUT, both untied from TRK_OUT; the loop regulates when IMON_OUT reaches
    1.208 V (1.187 to 1.229), with I(IMON_OUT) = gm x V(sense), gm 1.00 mmho (0.94 to 1.085, E and I grades over
    temperature, characterised at VCSPOUT 5.025 V only: at 15.1 V it is a bench item, T-P3). R17 (IMON_OUT to
    ground, 10k as generated) at 24.3 k 1 percent. The worst case also takes TRK_OUT at its highest: FBOUT 1.222 V
    (1.193 to 1.222, page 4) on R10 115k and R11 10.0k at 1 percent (gen_sch_e.py:576) gives 15.56 V (15.09 V typical),
    and the stage at this record's low efficiency bracket, 0.90. Into the stage, W:
  RSENSE2 mOhm  limit A low / typ / high  W in at 15.1 V, 0.93: low / typ / high  worst W, 15.56 V, 0.93  worst W, 15.56 V, 0.90  holds 100 W at every worst
  ------------  ------------------------  --------------------------------------  ----------------------  ----------------------  --------------------------
  8.0           5.52 / 6.21 / 6.86        90 / 101 / 111                          114.8                   118.6                   NO                        
  9.1           4.85 / 5.46 / 6.03        79 / 89 / 98                            100.9                   104.3                   NO                        
  10.0          4.41 / 4.97 / 5.49        72 / 81 / 89                            91.8                    94.9                    yes                       
      The least RSENSE2 that holds 100 W at every worst is 9.49 mOhm. Setting (ii) is therefore 10.0 mOhm: at most
      94.9 W into the stage in every worst case, 81 W typical, 72 W at its low end. 8.0 mOhm is 100 W only
      typically; 9.1 mOhm (this record's second issue) reaches 100.9 W at 0.93 and 104.3 W at 0.90 at the worst.
      With the bus held lower (a vehicle at 9 to 15 V) the limit is a lower power, which the vehicle then covers.
      Parts: one 2512 sense resistor, R17's value, two pins untied, under 2 EUR. At setting (ii) the stage draws at
      most 5.39 A at 17.6 V or above, inside PV_P's declared 5.68 A; the peak (the panel's short-circuit current, a
      fault) rises from 6.25 to about 12.5 A, so F2 and J_SOLAR are still re-rated for a 200 Wp panel (at 1.25 times,
      about 15.6 A, as route A). The constant-power front end against a current-limited source is the case the
      design already has whenever the panel gives less than the front end draws (gen_sch_e.py:99-103); the host
      contract (FW-A16) must hold it.

6f. An external DC source on the 9 to 36 V entry, as an OPTION and not the mission's basis: the entry guarantees
    4.85 A (carries 6.15 A) through F1 10 A, the LM74700 diode, the LM5069 hot-swap and the choke into board A's
    front end, chain 0.911 to the node. At 12 V the guaranteed 4.85 A is 58 W at the source and 53 W at the node,
    above every state M1 uses (42.8 W needs 3.9 A at 12 V, 2.0 A at 24 V at the source). Energy a source must
    give per night, the sun-down hours of section 3 (September 11.3 h, December 16.2 h; by day the panel's
    shortfall against the load is on top of it, section 5b's 'h sun < load'):
  state           W     September night Wh from the source  Ah at 12 V  Ah of a 12.8 V LiFePO4  December night Wh  Ah at 12 V
  --------------  ----  ----------------------------------  ----------  ----------------------  -----------------  ----------
  PS-IDLE-SPEC    42.8  529.6                               44.1        41.4                    759.7              63.3      
  PS-RED2         31.4  388.3                               32.4        30.3                    557.0              46.4      
  PS-SURV-R       23.3  288.0                               24.0        22.5                    413.0              34.4      
